<title>CHINA: CHINA FREEZES PROFITS IN AUGUST RUBBER CONTRACT.</title>
<headline>CHINA FREEZES PROFITS IN AUGUST RUBBER CONTRACT.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The China Commodity Futures Exchange in southern Hainan province said it has from Thursday temporarily frozen profits generated from offsetting the August rubber contract, an exchange statement said.</p>
<p>It did not say how long the freeze would remain in effect. The return of margin payments on liquidated positions in the August contract would also be delayed, the statement said.</p>
<p>The price of the August rubber contract fluctuated sharply due to a short squeeze before the exchange worked out a series of clampdown measures.</p>
<p>The measures included barring investors from building new positions in the August contract and lifting margin requirements.</p>
<p>The contract will start delivery from August 18.</p>
<p>-- Shanghai Newsroom (86) 21-6279 7004</p>
</text>
